        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was founded in 1857 within Hardin Township, marking its early growth in central Illinois.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1910 slogan captured its spirit: \"Time marches on 1857‑2007,\" celebrating a century of community life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A bandstand built in 1906‑07 became the heart of local music, hosting popular brass band concerts for decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The bandstand sits on the square beside the shelter house, a classic example of a public park gazebo.",
